@@ -0,0 +1,186 @@
+## Qualify BOLT's second-stage cache-directed hot/warm/cold splitting on a
+## relocation-complete Cortex-M image.  This is distinct from Profile2: a
+## cover-call benefit moves five nonzero-count blocks to the warm fragment,
+## while one zero-count block remains cold.
+
+# RUN: split-file %s %t
+# RUN: llvm-mc -filetype=obj -triple thumbv7m-none-eabi -mcpu=cortex-m3 \
+# RUN:   %t/fixture.s -o %t/fixture.o
+# RUN: ld.lld --emit-relocs -T %t/link.ld %t/fixture.o -o %t/reference.elf
+
+## ARM runs LongJmp, whose ordinary model handles at most two fragments.
+## Reject CDSplit cleanly unless the caller selects its compatible compact
+## branch model; never leave this as a debug-build assertion.
+# RUN: not llvm-bolt %t/reference.elf --firmbolt-cortex-m-cpu=cortex-m3 \
+# RUN:   --data=%t/profile.fdata --relocs --use-old-text \
